  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115996",
      "title": "How NOT To Provide A Service",
      "lectureOrder": 178,
      "videoOrder": 170,
      "sourceHash": "61788d8de75d194d99e7bab0d7e6aaa3d421f813cd18c22a3622bdb266fba1a3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 3.21,
          "en": "So, how can we make this TasksService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.21,
          "end": 6.42,
          "en": "available in this NewTaskComponent?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.42,
          "end": 9.06,
          "en": "Well, since it is a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.06,
          "end": 11.46,
          "en": "we can instantiate that class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.46,
          "end": 14.55,
          "en": "to create an object based on that class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.55,
          "end": 16.74,
          "en": "That's not Angular-specific,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.74,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "but in general how you can work with classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 21.903,
          "en": "in JavaScript and TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.98,
          "end": 24.96,
          "en": "So here, we could add the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.96,
          "end": 27.45,
          "en": "to the NewTaskComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.45,
          "end": 30.54,
          "en": "and also add a new private property, maybe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.54,
          "end": 33.723,
          "en": "which we could call tasksService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.76,
          "end": 38.377,
          "en": "which should be of type TasksService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.05,
          "end": 43.71,
          "en": "And for that, I'm importing my TasksService class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 46.353,
          "en": "so that I can use the class name as a type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.64,
          "end": 48.99,
          "en": "And then in the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.99,
          "end": 52.23,
          "en": "we can initialize this tasksService property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.23,
          "end": 55.533,
          "en": "by instantiating the TasksService like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.03,
          "end": 59.49,
          "en": "This is how we could make it available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.49,
          "end": 61.53,
          "en": "And now in onAddTask,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.53,
          "end": 65.25,
          "en": "we could call this tasksService.addTask,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.25,
          "end": 67.87,
          "en": "and then pass our data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.2,
          "end": 72.423,
          "en": "like this to addTask.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.28,
          "end": 79.28,
          "en": "Or, since I have equal property and value names here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.5,
          "end": 81.78,
          "en": "I can also use this shorter notation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.78,
          "end": 84.513,
          "en": "which is supported by JavaScript and TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.4,
          "end": 88.74,
          "en": "That is how we could use this service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.74,
          "end": 92.253,
          "en": "But this approach has one major problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.12,
          "end": 94.53,
          "en": "With this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.53,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "we have an instance for the NewTaskComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 100.02000000000001,
          "en": "and if I then want to use that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.02000000000001,
          "end": 103.38,
          "en": "and that service therefore in another component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.38,
          "end": 106.14,
          "en": "in the TasksListComponent, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.14,
          "end": 109.143,
          "en": "I have to create a separate instance there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.1,
          "end": 112.71000000000001,
          "en": "And therefore, this separate instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.71000000000001,
          "end": 115.32,
          "en": "wouldn't contain the tasks I'm adding here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 117.9,
          "en": "in the NewTaskComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.9,
          "end": 121.89,
          "en": "I would be working with two separate instances of the class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.89,
          "end": 125.1,
          "en": "and therefore, I would not be sharing data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.1,
          "end": 127.17,
          "en": "And hence, we would have a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.17,
          "end": 129.093,
          "en": "that is absolutely useless.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.32,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "That's why we want to use one and the same instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 136.98,
          "en": "of our class object in both Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.98,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "and that is where Angular's dependency injection mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 141.663,
          "en": "comes into play.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
